Kuwait City already lives with a condition many other cities may soon face: urban life sustained not by natural freshwater sources, but by desalination, wastewater reuse and energy-intensive infrastructure. As climate change and population growth reshape urban water security, Kuwait’s experience offers lessons that extend well beyond the Middle East.

